# Provenance — charts/README.md § `SOURCE` is required, including when nothing was forked.
#
# ADR-010: "Their charts are a starting point, not a dependency. Where a chart is close, fork it into
# charts/ with the upstream commit recorded in a SOURCE file." Nothing was forked here, and
# `vendored: none` is an answer to "where did this come from" where a missing file is not.

vendored: none
upstream: https://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs-operator

# The upstream API this chart's template targets. ⚠ An API group/version, not a commit: nothing is
# vendored, so there is no upstream tree to pin.
upstream-api: seaweed.seaweedfs.com/v1

engine: https://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs

# ⚠ THE FIELD LIST BELOW IS INHERITED FROM charts/managed/seaweedfs/SOURCE'S REVIEW OF 2026-08-12
# AND WAS NOT RE-READ AGAINST UPSTREAM ON THIS DATE. That review recorded, from
# `api/v1/seaweed_types.go` and its siblings, that the operator ships twelve CRDs beside `Seaweed`
# and that `BucketSpec` is:
#
#     (name, clusterRef, reclaimPolicy, adoptExisting, versioning, objectLock, quota, owner,
#      access, placement, anonymousRead)
#
# — "docs/plan/15 § The resource model's child types almost one to one". This chart renders FOUR of
# those eleven and the seven omissions are each argued at
# `StorageBuckets.Schema2026`'s remarks in src/Providers/CyberCloud.Providers.Storage.
#
# ⚠ WHAT THAT MEANS FOR A READER, STATED RATHER THAN IMPLIED: `spec.clusterRef` is rendered as a
# STRING naming the Seaweed in the same namespace, and the recorded review names the field without
# giving its Go type. If upstream spells it as an object (`{name, namespace}`) rather than a string,
# every Bucket this chart renders is refused by the CRD's own schema at apply time — visibly, per
# object, with the API server's own message, which is the failure mode this platform prefers to a
# silent one. It is called out here because a field list is weaker evidence than a struct, and
# saying which claim is weak is the point of this file.
inherited-review: charts/managed/seaweedfs/SOURCE, reviewed 2026-08-12

# ⚠ RE-READ 2026-09-15 AGAINST `api/v1/bucket_types.go` AT seaweedfs-operator-0.1.38 — THE TAG
# charts/bundle/seaweedfs-operator PINS — AND THE PARAGRAPH ABOVE WAS RIGHT TO BE WORRIED. THREE OF THE
# FOUR RENDERED FIELDS HAD THE WRONG SHAPE, and every Bucket this chart rendered for a month would have
# been refused by the real CRD's schema. The stub the cluster suite derived had an open schema, which
# is why a month of green runs met no refusal — issue #91 closed that: the real definition is
# committed at charts/bundle/seaweedfs-operator/crds/buckets.seaweed.seaweedfs.com.yaml and both
# suites validate against it. What the struct actually says:
#
#   * `clusterRef` is `BucketClusterRef{name string (required, minLength 1), namespace string}` —
#     an OBJECT. Rendered `clusterRef: {name: …}` now.
#   * `versioning` is `VersioningState`, enum `Off | Enabled | Suspended`, `+kubebuilder:default:=Off`,
#     with an XValidation that it cannot return to Off. Rendered `Enabled`/`Off` from the boolean.
#     Turning the flag off after enabling is refused by the API server; conformance.yaml § owed,
#     `versioning-cannot-be-turned-off`.
#   * `quota` is `*BucketQuota{size resource.Quantity (required), enforce bool (default true)}` — an
#     OBJECT. Rendered `quota: {size: …}`, `enforce` left to its default.
#   * `name` is optional, pattern `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9.-]{1,61}[a-z0-9]$` — three characters minimum,
#     which is the S3 rule `name-grammar-is-wider-than-s3s` already records.
#
# The same read established `BucketStatus.usage` — `BucketUsage{objectCount int64, sizeBytes int64,
# lastUpdated *metav1.Time}` — written by `internal/controller/bucket_usage.go`'s refresher every five
# minutes from `collection.list`. That is what took `stats` off actions-without-handlers.txt.
reviewed: 2026-09-15 (bucket_types.go, bucket_usage.go, bucket_admin.go at seaweedfs-operator-0.1.38)

# ⚠ THE MUTATING WEBHOOK, WHICH IS WHY `StorageBuckets.Matches` IS CONTAINMENT RATHER THAN EQUALITY.
# `api/v1/seaweed_webhook.go` registers a defaulter whose body is a log line and
# `// TODO(user): fill in your defaulting logic.` It mutates nothing at the reviewed commit — so an
# equality comparison would pass against this operator and break silently against whichever release
# fills the TODO in, with the symptom being every bucket stuck in InProgress while its cluster is
# perfectly correct.
upstream-webhook: mutating, defaulter unimplemented as of 2026-08-12
